From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: advapi32: the event log functions talk to the Event Log service

OpenEventLog, RegisterEventSource, ReportEvent, ReadEventLog (sequential and
seek, forwards and backwards; whole records, ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER with
the size needed, ERROR_HANDLE_EOF), GetNumberOfEventLogRecords,
GetOldestEventLogRecord, GetEventLogInformation, ClearEventLog (with a
backup), BackupEventLog, OpenBackupEventLog (read from the file into memory;
ERROR_EVENTLOG_FILE_CORRUPT for anything else), NotifyChangeEventLog (a
thread waiting on the service) and CloseEventLog/DeregisterEventSource, as
clients of the service (0143). A name that is neither a log nor a registered
source opens Application. The A functions convert the records' names and
strings with the same layout. A handle is ours (log, source, read position);
a closed one is ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE. With the service unreachable a call
fails with RPC_S_SERVER_UNAVAILABLE after at most 3 s (then at once for 30 s)
-- ReportEvent never hangs a program. ReportEvent's strings still go to the
debug log as before.

advapi32:eventlog: the tests that now pass lose their todo_wine; the two
that need ten records in System are todo only while it has fewer.
506 tests, 0 failures (14 todo: ETW, not this).

Gate: test/eventlog-gate.sh.
